  "notes": "USAGE:\nComposed of {点|てん} (to light, to turn on) and {滅|めつ} (to extinguish, to turn off). Describes the on-off cycle of lights, not continuous illumination.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {点滅|てんめつ}する (to flash, to blink)\n- {点滅|てんめつ}{信号|しんごう} (flashing traffic signal)\n- {赤|あか}く{点滅|てんめつ}する (flash red)\n- {点滅|てんめつ}を{繰|く}り{返|かえ}す (flash repeatedly)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {明滅|めいめつ}: flickering — more literary; describes light wavering between bright and dim\n- {点灯|てんとう}: lighting up — turning a light on (without the off cycle)\n- {消灯|しょうとう}: lights out — turning lights off",
